MiaUI modifications vs upstream cobaltgit/Butterscotch (pinned at
92ed6b8c3766361a201a69d202bcde5873cdad7e - the same commit as the Undertale
MiaUI port):

- patches/001-rg35xx-fallback-mapping.patch (new): createFallbackMappings()
  for the RG35XX gpio-keys pad (dpad at sdl 13-16, volume key at 12)
- patches/002-chunklog.patch, patches/003-stage-markers.patch,
  patches/004-sdl-error.patch, patches/005-sdl1-error.patch,
  patches/006-fpslog.patch: diagnostics (chunk/stage/FPSLOG markers,
  SDL_GetError() in init failures)
- patches/007-joyname-cache.patch: cache SDL_JoystickName() per slot
  (SDL 1.2 opens the device + issues ioctls every call; ~50ms/frame)
- patches/008-exit-cursor.patch: Select + Start held together quits
  cleanly; the fbcon stub cursor (which never moves and sits in a corner)
  is always hidden
- patches/009-am2r-string-placeholder.patch: backport of Butterscotch
  c1260061 "support placeholder substitution in string()" (issue #486) -
  without it every AM2R formatted string renders as "[!]"; adapted to the
  pinned tree's APIs (single-arg RValue_toString, freed by the patch)
- Dockerfile retargeted to arm-buildroot-linux-gnueabihf (glibc 2.37,
  INTERP /lib/ld-linux-armhf.so.3), SDL1.2 fbcon + ALSA, software renderer,
  WAD 14-only interpreter build (AM2R is a GM:S 1.4 WAD-14 game)
- launch.sh: ROMs/Ports/AM2R.pak/ layout, SDL_VIDEODRIVER=fbcon,
  SDL_NOMOUSE=1, CPU governor pinning, debug.log probe

The pin matches the Undertale port (not the newer ButterscotchRunner
upstream) on purpose: that upstream has deleted the software renderer this
port requires, while the pin's one AM2R-critical gap (string() placeholder
substitution) is covered by patch 009.

Upstream code retains its own licenses; see upstream/LICENSE (AGPLv3).
Upstream is vendored under upstream/ and is re-cloneable at the pinned
commit (see .gitignore).

AM2R game files, artwork and audio are the property of DoctorM64 and the
AM2R community team (Metroid II itself is Nintendo property) and are not
covered by the project license.
